Rendering optimization
Earlier in this chapter, we saw that a React component is rerendered when its state changes.
A component is also rerendered when its props change. It is important to understand that
child components are rerendered when their parent component re-renders. So, changing
some state could be an expensive change if there are lots of components that contain lots of
elements that get rerendered as a result.
